@baseUrl = http://localhost:5087

### Criar mock simples (GET com body estático)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/users",
  "statusCode": 200,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "description": "Lista todos os usuários",
  "responseBody": {
    "items": [
      { "id": 1, "name": "Alice" },
      { "id": 2, "name": "Bob" }
    ]
  }
}

### Criar mock com variáveis de template (POST que ecoa dados do body)
# Nota: {{uuid}} e {{$.x}} são variáveis do RestMock, não do REST Client.
# A extensão REST Client pode exibir avisos, mas envia o corpo corretamente.
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "POST",
  "pattern": "/api/users",
  "statusCode": 201,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "id": "{{uuid}}",
    "name": "{{$.name}}",
    "email": "{{$.email}}"
  }
}

### Criar mock com pattern tipado na URL
# Nota: {{uuid}} é variável do RestMock — ver comentário acima.
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/users/{guid}",
  "statusCode": 200,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "description": "Busca usuário por ID",
  "responseBody": {
    "id": "{{uuid}}",
    "name": "Alice"
  }
}

### Criar mock com query string tipada
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/products?category=[string]&page=[int]",
  "statusCode": 200,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "page": 1,
    "items": []
  }
}

### Criar mock que simula timeout (delay de 60s + 504)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/reports",
  "statusCode": 504,
  "processingTime": 60000,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "error": "Gateway Timeout"
  }
}

### Criar mock que simula erro de autenticação
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/protected",
  "statusCode": 401,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "error": "Unauthorized"
  }
}

### Criar mock com curinga de versão e path opcional
POST {{baseUrl}}/mocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/v*/health",
  "statusCode": 200,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "status": "ok"
  }
}

### Listar todos os mocks cadastrados
GET {{baseUrl}}/mocks

### Buscar mock por ID (substitua o guid pelo id retornado no POST)
GET {{baseUrl}}/mocks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Atualizar mock por ID (substitua o guid pelo id retornado no POST)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/mocks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "pattern": "/api/users",
  "statusCode": 200,
  "processingTime": 0,
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "responseBody": {
    "items": []
  }
}

### Excluir mock por ID (substitua o guid pelo id a ser removido)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/mocks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
